{
    // Standard NAV-priced ask (the shell). No specs and no off-chain code exist yet.
    // An ZC_Standard_SaleOrder with one more condition on a fill: a pricing expression the seller chose
    // must also pass. The expression works a price out of on-chain state, so the seller never
    // updates the ask. A new way to price is a new expression, not a new ask contract.
    // ZC_Standard_AccruedValue_Pricing is the first: a bond's accrued value plus or minus a margin.
    // Nothing here verifies what the token is: a buyer, or a buying contract, does that.
    //
    // CONSTANTS
    // CONST_PAYMENT_TOKEN: Coll[Byte] - the asset the seller is paid in; EMPTY for ERG. One address
    //   per payment asset under one shared template, as for ZC_Standard_SaleOrder. The pricing expression
    //   must be compiled for the same asset; this script cannot check that.
    //
    // TOKENS
    // tokens(0): (token for sale, amount remaining) - the only token allowed
    //
    // REGISTERS (all present; all copied unchanged to the continuation)
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the seller script: is paid, may cancel
    // R5: Coll[Long] - 4..64 values:
    //   0, 1 floor price, numerator and denominator, both positive. A fill of u raw units pays at
    //     least ceil(u * numerator / denominator) whatever the expression says. It is the seller's
    //     backstop against an expression that misprices; numerator 1 with a large denominator
    //     switches it off.
    //   2 minimum fill; a smaller fill is allowed only when it takes everything that is left
    //   3 expiry height; fills require HEIGHT < expiry, and from then on anyone may refund
    //   4.. payload read only by the pricing expression
    // R6: Coll[Byte] - blake2b256 of the serialized pricing expression
    // R7: Coll[Byte] - payload read only by the pricing expression; EMPTY if it needs none
    //
    // FILL (anyone, before expiry)
    // Context var 0: Int payout index. 1: Int continuation index, absent for a full take.
    // 2: Coll[Byte] the pricing expression. Vars 3 and up belong to the expression.
    // Payout (the ask convention, shared with ZC_Standard_SaleOrder): at the seller script, R4 = SELF.id,
    //   R5: Long = the raw units this payout pays for. For a token price the payment token is the
    //   payout's tokens(0), and the buyer funds the box's nanoERG.
    // Continuation: this script, R4 to R7 unchanged, value not lower, tokens(0) = what is left.
    // The expression runs with this box as SELF. It re-reads vars 0 and 1 and must itself require
    // the payout to hold its price: this script only enforces the floor.
    //
    // EXPIRY REFUND (anyone, once HEIGHT >= expiry)
    // As ZC_Standard_SaleOrder. Var 0 names the refund: at the seller script, R4 = SELF.id, every token of
    // this box, and at least 1000000 nanoERG (all of the value, if less). nanoERG funded above
    // 1000000 is the batcher's fee and survives partial fills. This matters more here than for a
    // fixed price: the ask stops filling once its bond settles or matures, while it still holds
    // the unit or shares needed to claim the settlement.
    //
    // CANCEL
    // A co-spent box guarded by the seller script releases this box at any height.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS
    // - The seller inspects the pricing expression. Its hash is a commitment, not a proof that it
    //   prices well: an always-true expression leaves only the floor.
    // - The batcher fee is the buyer's to set. This order pays none.
    // - Storage rent, serialization and maximum cost are unverified.

    val sellerHash = SELF.R4[Coll[Byte]].get
    val sellerAuth = INPUTS.exists { (b: Box) =>
        b.id != SELF.id && blake2b256(b.propositionBytes) == sellerHash
    }

    if (sellerAuth) {
        sigmaProp(true)
    } else {
        val terms = SELF.R5[Coll[Long]].get
        val payoutIndex = getVar[Int](0).get
        val nextIndex = getVar[Int](1)
        if (terms.size < 4 || terms.size > 64 || SELF.tokens.size != 1 ||
            payoutIndex < 0 || payoutIndex >= OUTPUTS.size) {
            sigmaProp(false)
        } else if (HEIGHT.toLong >= terms(3)) {
            // Expiry refund, by anyone, exactly as ZC_Standard_SaleOrder: the tokens go back to the seller,
            // and the batcher's fee is whatever nanoERG the seller funded above 1000000.
            val refund = OUTPUTS(payoutIndex)
            sigmaProp(
                blake2b256(refund.propositionBytes) == sellerHash &&
                refund.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                refund.tokens == SELF.tokens &&
                (refund.value >= 1000000L || refund.value >= SELF.value)
            )
        } else {
            val numerator = terms(0)
            val denominator = terms(1)
            val minFill = terms(2)
            val have = SELF.tokens(0)._2
            val payout = OUTPUTS(payoutIndex)
            val pricingHash = SELF.R6[Coll[Byte]].get
            val payload = SELF.R7[Coll[Byte]].get

            val continued = if (nextIndex.isDefined) {
                val index = nextIndex.get
                if (index < 0 || index >= OUTPUTS.size || index == payoutIndex) {
                    false
                } else {
                    val next = OUTPUTS(index)
                    next.propositionBytes == SELF.propositionBytes &&
                    next.value >= SELF.value &&
                    next.tokens.size == 1 &&
                    next.tokens(0)._1 == SELF.tokens(0)._1 &&
                    next.tokens(0)._2 >= 1L && next.tokens(0)._2 < have &&
                    next.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == sellerHash &&
                    next.R5[Coll[Long]].get == terms &&
                    next.R6[Coll[Byte]].get == pricingHash &&
                    next.R7[Coll[Byte]].get == payload
                }
            } else true

            if (!continued || numerator <= 0L || denominator <= 0L) {
                sigmaProp(false)
            } else {
                val remaining = if (nextIndex.isDefined) OUTPUTS(nextIndex.get).tokens(0)._2 else 0L
                val sold = have - remaining
                val floorPrice = (sold.toBigInt * numerator.toBigInt + denominator.toBigInt - 1L.toBigInt) /
                    denominator.toBigInt
                // An empty collection taken from the box, not a literal: testing the constant alone
                // is folded at compile time and would give each payment asset a different template.
                val noToken = SELF.id.slice(0, 0)
                val paid = if (CONST_PAYMENT_TOKEN == noToken) {
                    payout.value
                } else if (payout.tokens.size > 0 && payout.tokens(0)._1 == CONST_PAYMENT_TOKEN) {
                    payout.tokens(0)._2
                } else 0L

                sigmaProp(
                    sold >= 1L && (sold >= minFill || remaining == 0L) &&
                    blake2b256(payout.propositionBytes) == sellerHash &&
                    payout.R4[Coll[Byte]].get == SELF.id &&
                    payout.R5[Long].get == sold &&
                    paid.toBigInt >= floorPrice &&
                    blake2b256(getVar[Coll[Byte]](2).get) == pricingHash
                ) && executeFromVar[SigmaProp](2)
            }
        }
    }
}
